  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining on September 10th. An idea submission phase for AI-enhanced data visualization tools was open until July 20th. The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing, celebrated on October 10th. Subsequent phases include user interface enhancements starting in October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. The executive board approved a total budget of $2 million for all phases, and a specific $15,000 budget for training programs has been approved for the coding team and project managers, with sessions starting next month."
